Subject: [PATCH] phy: qcom-qmp-pcie: honor the BCR bypass during teardown

The existing Piano BCR bypass guards the normal PHY initialization reset,
but error unwind and PHY exit still assert the same bulk BCR. The board
has no phy_nocsr reset, so a full PCIe suspend reaches that assertion via
host deinit and phy_power_off even when piano_skip_bcr is enabled.

Apply the existing bypass to both remaining bulk reset assertions. Keep
the no-CSR reset path and clock/regulator teardown unchanged.

---
--- a/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-pcie.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-pcie.c
@@ -5767,7 +5767,7 @@
 	return 0;
 
 err_assert_reset:
-	if (!qmp->skip_init)
+	if (!qmp->skip_init && !piano_skip_bcr)
 		reset_control_bulk_assert(cfg->num_resets, qmp->resets);
 err_disable_regulators:
 	regulator_bulk_disable(cfg->num_vregs, qmp->vregs);
@@ -5782,7 +5782,7 @@
 
 	if (qmp->nocsr_reset)
 		reset_control_assert(qmp->nocsr_reset);
-	else
+	else if (!piano_skip_bcr)
 		reset_control_bulk_assert(cfg->num_resets, qmp->resets);
 
 	clk_bulk_disable_unprepare(ARRAY_SIZE(qmp_pciephy_clk_l), qmp->clks);
